// Decimal to double conversion, pinned as an exact mantissa times a power of two so the formatter cannot mask a
// parse error. 9.3.1 fixes one answer for at most 20 significant digits: nearest, ties to even. These inputs sit
// within 2^-125 of a rounding midpoint, which is as close as 20 digits can come without landing on one, so they
// are what a conversion that rounds on anything less than exact arithmetic gets wrong. The old double-double
// engine failed a fifth of Numbstrict's set of them. See docs/notes/Todo.md and Numbstrict's docs/RealConversion.md.
> function pow2(g) { var v = 1, i; for (i = 0; i < g; ++i) v *= 2; for (i = 0; i > g; --i) v /= 2; return v }
